From ea336bc314afa8aec93d630493d3d2a1ba15e86b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 18:54:21 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 08/19] Replay real Base calls through the verifier's Base EVM
 from pinned witnesses

The witness gateway keys the bare block hash newer alloy sends as well as the
EIP-1898 object, and can offer a subset of methods so a recording without the
access-list hint replays deterministically. The e2e suite checks Base-EVM
execution against the chain's own node and refusal beyond the validated Denim
horizon; the replay suite recomputes recorded mainnet eth_call results offline
and fails closed on a missing witness or a stale latest head.

(cherry picked from commit eb707adc0e52050f38ba7352865bcba24b6f6d2e)
